The "peak of the little Black River" is the highest mountain in Mauritius, at 828 metres. It belongs to the Black River range, above the national park.

The most common route starts from Plaine Champagne on the plateau; other routes begin near Chamarel and at the national park's visitor centre on the Black River side. A bench known as "Bench 828" marks the summit, which looks out over the forest and down to the lagoons of the west coast.

## Good to know

- The final section is steep and exposed in places: hike only in dry weather, with good shoes.
- Going with a local guide is a good idea if you do not know the area.
